<title>CANADA: COM DEV wins C$20 mln follow-up contract.</title>
<headline>COM DEV wins C$20 mln follow-up contract.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Ontario 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>COM DEV International Ltd said on Monday it signed a C$20 million contract with Motorola Inc's satellite communications division to produce 30 sets of Ka-band antennas for the IRIDIUM global personal communications system.</p>
<p>COM DEV said delivery of the antennas is scheduled to begin in the first quarter of 1998.</p>
<p>Under two previous contracts, COM DEV designed and is manufacturing the antennas for all 72 of the IRIDIUM prototype and operational satellites, COM DEV said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
